# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data
#
# Everything under data/demo/ is produced by `python scripts/build_data.py`
# from a fixed seed, so it is reproducible byte-for-byte and does not belong in
# version control. The seven GeoTIFFs alone are ~45 MB, and the previews add
# another ~20 MB, which would dominate the repository and make every clone slow
# for no benefit.
#
# The generator scripts ARE tracked, which is what matters: anyone can run
# build_data.py and get identical scenes, then verify_scenes.py proves they
# match the recorded ground truth.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/demo/*.tif
data/demo/previews/
data/demo/truth.json
data/demo/manifest.json
data/demo/rainfall_supaul.csv

# Real imagery from Bhoonidhi (NRSC / ISRO).
#
# The raw product directories are ~420 MB each and hold single-band BAND2/3/4/5
# GeoTIFFs plus BAND_META.txt -- 3.4 GB for eight scenes, and nothing reads them
# after ingest_liss3.py has run. Those stay out.
#
# data/real/converted/ IS tracked: eight 4-band GeoTIFFs, 10-17 MB each, 102 MB
# total. Unlike data/demo/ these cannot be regenerated -- they came from a
# Bhoonidhi account behind a login -- so the only way a teammate gets real ISRO
# imagery is from the repository. scripts/verify_real.py reads them.
#
# Note the pattern: `data/real/*` excludes the CONTENTS, not the directory. A
# trailing-slash `data/real/` would stop git descending into it at all and the
# negation below could never re-include anything.
data/real/*
!data/real/converted/

# Runtime evidence ledger. Created on first query, grows per session, and is
# machine-local state rather than source.
data/ledger.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Screenshots regenerated by scripts/ui_check.py on every run.
docs/screens/

